  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local liaison support Fish Farmer Field School Sidoarjo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In and around Sidoarjo, a Fish Farmer Field School (FFFS) is operated, involving local communities and fishermen. The FFFS project started in July 2024 and is expected to conclude in June 2025.The FFFS, piloted in two different villages, aims to create know-how, awareness and capacity on the contribution of nature-based solutions (NbS) to improving both aquaculture and water quality issues in two local communities as well as in the regency&#x2019;s institutions and organisations related to aquaculture. This assignment aims to assign the capacity of a local liaison to regularly coordinate with the team implementing the FFFS as well as the governmental organisations of East Java Province (e.g. Planning department of the Sidoarjo Regency, Bappeda Sidoarjo; Department of Water Resources of East Java Province, PUSDA Jawa Timur) on the progress, outcomes and potential uptake of the FFFS concept. Among this are stakeholder discussions regarding alternative locations and financial sustainability of the FFFS concept.</narrative>
  </description>
